 "author_id_missing": false,
 "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/17423967/my-char-pointer-points-to-invalid-value-after-being-cast-from-int",
 "body_html": "<p>I am learning C programming language, I have just started learning <strong>arrays with pointers</strong>. I have problem in this question, I hope the that output must be <strong><code>5</code></strong> but it is <strong><code>2</code></strong>, Can anyone please explain why?</p>\n\n<pre><code>int main(){\n   int arr[] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};\n   char *ptr = (char *) arr;\n   printf(\"%d\", *(ptr+4));\n   return 0;\n}\n</code></pre>\n",
 "passes": [
